WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
At Cape Canaveral, the Courier Communication Satellite is viewed before its launching into

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.120
orbit. The 51-inch sphere, packed with 300 pounds of equipment, is carried into orbit

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:17.960
by a Thor-Able star missile, currently the workhorse of American deep space research.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:22.960
This will be the 100th successful firing of the Thor missile, and it will carry into orbit

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:37.320
a satellite even more remarkable than the recent Echo. Unlike the Echo, which mirrors

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:42.120
back Earth's transmissions, the Courier is equipped to receive and rebroadcast messages

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:47.040
from the ground. Marking the third anniversary of the space age, Courier relayed a message

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:52.520
from the President to the United Nations, a major stride toward a new worldwide communication

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:58.680
system.
